Docs say sink objects accept args, arguments, indices, or all; we now support parameters too but no need.

Potential markdown issue: code block config uses single-quoted key at top in JS object? `'security/detect-taint': [...]` is valid statement? As standalone code block not meant run, okay. Prettier markdown might format but check passed.

Need maybe mention `reportLocation` in docs? We implemented but not documented. Could add one line. Not necessary but feature API. Add:
- `reportLocation`: `'sink'` (default) or `'call'` for cross-function call site.
Also options schema allows. Good.

Need maybe add alias exports to types? `plugin.utils` not typed. Hidden TS tests unlikely. But our package `lint:types` runs `tsc` on types dir only and `attw --pack`. It might not check index.js. `types/index.d.ts` declares plugin object exactly and doesn't include utils. TypeScript consumers using `plugin.utils` would get type error because declared type has no utils. We should update type declaration to include optional or required utils. Since runtime always has, add:
```
utils: {
 taintTracker: Rule.RuleModule & { ... }?
}
```
But our taintTracker module is rule object plus extra functions. For TypeScript, easiest:
```
utils: {
  taintTracker: Rule.RuleModule & Record<string, unknown>;
};
```
Need import Rule already. The declared const plugin type currently:
```
declare const plugin: Required<Pick<ESLint.Plugin,'meta'>> & {
 meta...
